/****************************************************************************
 * Contest 2026 team 236 - Anime Voice Companion
 *
 * anime_voice_main.c - application entry point.
 *
 * Brings up LVGL on the Gemini-S1 panel (/dev/lcd0), then wires the UI, the
 * Wi-Fi helper and the push-to-talk voice loop together:
 *
 *      +--------+   PTT down    +-----------+   ASR text   +-----------+
 *      |  idle  |-------------->| listening |------------->| thinking  |
 *      +--------+               +-----------+              +-----------+
 *            ^                                                |
 *            |            TTS finished                        | LLM reply
 *            |                                                v
 *            |   +------------------------------------+  +-----------+
 *            +---|              speaking              |<-|  reply    |
 *                +------------------------------------+  +-----------+
 *
 * Everything that blocks on the network (ASR / LLM / TTS) runs on the
 * ai_agent worker threads.  Their callbacks only stash a result into a small
 * mutex protected slot; the LVGL timer at 30 ms drains it and is therefore
 * the only place that touches widget state.
 *
 * When the Vela AI Agent is not reachable the app still works as a demo:
 * a tap on the character returns a line from the built-in offline persona
 * table, and the status bar keeps showing the Wi-Fi state.
 ****************************************************************************/

